 8. The trial Court decreed the suit in part. It was held that the mortgage deed and the sanction letter was the contract between the parties and the conditions of the mortgage deed are binding on the plaintiffs. On appeal the appellate court below dismissed the appeal of the Corporation and allowed the cross-appeal filed by the Respondents and accordingly decreed the suit in full. The appellate court noticed that certain terms and conditions mentioned in the "mortgage deed" is contrary to that of the sanctioned letters." In this view it was found "that the findings of the learned Munsif "that the sanctioning letter and Rehani deed together form contract is not correct."
